# TypeConstructor qualified leaf preservation: nominal ADT constructors carry qualified
# tags that preserve nominal identity through alias expansion.
#
# expand_all_tycon_apps distinguishes two forms of TypeConstructor:
#   - Bare (transient): TypeConstructor { name } where !name.contains('.') — expand
#   - Qualified (leaf): TypeConstructor { name } where name.contains('.') — preserve as-is
#
# Qualified constructor leaves (e.g., "Color.Red") stay after normalization.
# `TypeConstructor "Color.Red" <: TypeConstructor "Direction.Red"` is false by name inequality —
# nominal identity is preserved through the dot-qualified name in the expanded union body.
#
# At runtime: ADT constructors are injected as Variant values with qualified tags.
# Matching on them via `match` uses the qualified tag (Color.Red, Color.Green, Color.Blue).
# The runtime result verifies the correct variant was selected.
[
  Color: [type Red Green Blue]

  label: [fn [let c]
    [match c
      Color.Red:   "red"
      Color.Green: "green"
      Color.Blue:  "blue"
      _:           "unknown"]]

  r: [label Red]
  g: [label Green]
  b: [label Blue]
]
=== out
Dict({"Red": Variant(Color.Red, Null), "Green": Variant(Color.Green, Null), "Blue": Variant(Color.Blue, Null), "label": Function(c), "r": String("red"), "g": String("green"), "b": String("blue")})
